# Keep `git archive` output — which is what GitHub serves as a release
# tarball/zip — down to the theme payload ES actually loads.
#
# The documented install IS that archive — README.md tells the user to
# download the ZIP/tar.gz and drop it in themes/ — so this list is what
# lands on the SD card. Without it they would get the full history plus
# ~18 MB of docs/; with it, the theme itself and nothing else.
#
# LICENSE and CREDITS.md deliberately stay IN: the theme is CC-BY-NC-SA 2.0
# and derived from Ant's "XMB Menu ES-DE", so the attribution has to travel
# with the work. README.md stays for the install/customization instructions.
#
# Keep in sync with the --exclude list in scripts/deploy.sh's `sync`
# subcommand, which is the same decision for the on-device copy (it drops
# the three text files as well, since nothing reads them at runtime).
.github/            export-ignore
docs/               export-ignore
scripts/            export-ignore
docker/             export-ignore
tests/              export-ignore
.env.local.example  export-ignore
.gitignore          export-ignore
.gitattributes      export-ignore
